You are a senior QA automation architect. Rebuild this project folder into a professional, cost-efficient, self-learning QA agent framework for Claude Code, also usable by Devin and GitHub Copilot.

The agent behaves like a fellow QA engineer who received KT. It learns from every document I give it, remembers it, questions me on gaps and contradictions, designs tests, executes them, delivers a test case document with status, steps, and proof, and can update my separate automation framework repo when I ask.

I will never use slash commands. Infer intent from plain prompts.

====================================
PHASE 1: ANALYZE AND BACK UP
====================================
1. List every file and folder (knowledge, instructions, agents, skills, services/tools, configs, anything else).
2. For each: purpose, empty/stub/useful, and whether it holds anything worth keeping (service code, MCP configs, KT content, secrets).
3. Safety net: git init if needed. Commit everything as "pre-rebuild snapshot" on branch backup/pre-rebuild. Copy the old tree to _archive/pre-rebuild/.
4. Report what you will keep and migrate, what you will discard, and the planned tree.
STOP and wait for my approval before wiping.

====================================
PHASE 2: WIPE AND REBUILD (after approval)
====================================
Delete the old structure (except _archive/, .git, and flagged service code/configs), then create:

